  "id": "attitude-survey",
  "term": "attitude survey",
  "definition": "An attitude survey is an assessment tool made up of questions or items used to measure people’s attitudes toward a particular subject, such as school science. In this context, it refers to an instrument designed to be easy to understand and administer while providing dependable measurement of those attitudes.",
